 "text": "Hi, how have you been? You do matter. Encourage her teacher, ask to sit in now and then, and show an interest in French books and songs. Would you like me to reword it? Then ask if you can sit in once her regular parents are busy with something else. Sing the lessons with her before bed, and buy the songs DVD. She might at first, especially if you only pop in now and then. If you become a regular, she'll probably get used to your voice. Help with the alphabet at first, then let her lead with games. You could ask her to teach you song while you two play together. Remember, you're supporting her learning, not competing with it.",
